  "body": " Plotting Legs   For each of the tables below record the number of legs in each group based on the number of animals present.     In a flock of geese (assume each goose has two legs)    Number of geese (G)  0  2  4  6  8  10  12  G    Number of legs (L)                In a pack of wolves (assume each wolf has four legs)    Number of wolves (W)  0  1  2  3  4  5  6  W    Number of legs (L)                In a group of octopuses (assume each octopus has eight legs)    Number of octopuses (C)  0  1  2  3  4  5  6  C    Number of legs (L)                Plot the ordered pairs for each of your tables on the graph below. Be sure to choose an appropriate scale for both axes. Label the axes.    Blank grid for plotting      "
